{"total_count":2,"incomplete_results":false,"items":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/issues/24792","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/issues/24792/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/issues/24792/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/issues/24792/events","html_url":"https://github.com/php/php-src/issues/24792","id":6062476605,"node_id":"I_kwDOAB0Los8AAAABaVoNPQ","number":24792,"title":"PHP 8.6: Assignment-result writes compile but fail with invalid opcode","user":{"login":"alwyn1024","id":2869280,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NjkyODA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2869280?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alwyn1024","html_url":"https://github.com/alwyn1024","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alwyn1024/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alwyn1024/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alwyn1024/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alwyn1024/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alwyn1024/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alwyn1024/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alwyn1024/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alwyn1024/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alwyn1024/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":148912283,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNDg5MTIyODM=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/labels/Bug","name":"Bug","color":"E99695","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":3611416941,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAB0Los7XQdlt","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/labels/Status:%20Needs%20Triage","name":"Status: Needs Triage","color":"D93F0B","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:36:30Z","updated_at":"2026-11-06T07:51:53Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Description\n\n## Summary\n\nIn PHP 8.6.0RC4, writing to an array dimension on an assignment result compiles successfully, but execution fails with an `Invalid opcode` fatal error.\n\nPHP 8.5.10 rejects the same construct during compilation.\n\n## Minimal reproducer\n\n```php\n<?php\n($a = [1])[0] = 2;\nvar_dump($a);\n```\n\n### Actual behavior\n\n**PHP 8.5.10:** Compilation fails:\n\n```\nFatal error: Cannot use temporary expression in write context\n```\n\n**PHP 8.6.0RC4:** `php -l` succeeds, but executing the code fails:\n\n```\nFatal error: Invalid opcode 23/2/1.\n```\n\n### Reference-assignment control\n\n```php\n<?php\n$b = [1];\n($a =& $b)[0] = 2;\nvar_dump($a, $b);\n```\n\nPHP 8.6.0RC4 accepts and executes this successfully, with both arrays containing `[2]`.\n\nOther assignment-derived property writes, destructuring-result writes, compound assignments, `unset`, and reference-binding operations exhibit related discrepancies.\n\n## Expected behavior / clarification requested\n\nShould assignment-derived dimension and property writes be rejected during compilation, or should PHP generate valid writable operands for these expressions?\n\nIn particular, is the ordinary-assignment failure a compiler emission defect, a missing compile-time rejection, or an intentional distinction between ordinary and reference-assignment results?\n\n## Affected versions\n\n- PHP 8.5.10 — Windows x64\n- PHP 8.6.0RC4 — Windows x64, NTS, VC2022\n- PHP 8.6 source commit: `f23b4c222cebe33be93ee8ecaaa14390c5507a08`\n\nThe PHP 8.6 executable was built from the specified source commit.\n\nReproduction: `php -n -l example.php`, followed by `php -n example.php`.\n\n## Relevant implementation\n\n- [[zend_compile_var_inner](https://github.com/php/php-src/blob/f23b4c222cebe33be93ee8ecaaa14390c5507a08/Zend/zend_compile.c#L12774)](https://github.com/php/php-src/blob/f23b4c222cebe33be93ee8ecaaa14390c5507a08/Zend/zend_compile.c#L12774)\n- [[ZEND_ASSIGN_DIM handlers](https://github.com/php/php-src/blob/f23b4c222cebe33be93ee8ecaaa14390c5507a08/Zend/zend_vm_def.h#L2680)](https://github.com/php/php-src/blob/f23b4c222cebe33be93ee8ecaaa14390c5507a08/Zend/zend_vm_def.h#L2680)\n- [[Related PR #20628](https://github.com/php/php-src/pull/20628)](https://github.com/php/php-src/pull/20628)\n\nThe compiler appears to allow assignment ASTs in writable contexts while producing operand kinds unsupported by the corresponding VM write handlers.\n\nI would appreciate clarification of the intended behavior before treating these forms as valid or invalid PHP source syntax.\n\n### PHP Version\n\n```plain\nPHP 8.6.0RC4 (cli) (built: Oct 25 2026 12:45:36) (NTS Visual C++ 2022 x64)\nCopyright © The PHP Group and Contributors\nZend Engine v4.6.0RC4, Copyright © Zend by Perforce\n    with Zend OPcache v8.6.0RC4, Copyright ©, by Zend by Perforce\n```\n\n### Operating System\n\nWindows x64 (64-bit), PHP 8.6.0RC4 NTS, Visual C++ 2022 (VC17)","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/issues/24792/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/issues/24792/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/issues/25046","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/issues/25046/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/issues/25046/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/issues/25046/events","html_url":"https://github.com/php/php-src/pull/25046","id":6112539680,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAB0Los8AAAABLrnuBQ","number":25046,"title":"Fix GH-24792: Assignment-result writes compile but fail with invalid opcode","user":{"login":"ChrisAbner","id":48162172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4MTYyMTcy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48162172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChrisAbner","html_url":"https://github.com/ChrisAbner","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChrisAbner/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChrisAbner/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChrisAbner/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChrisAbner/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChrisAbner/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChrisAbner/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChrisAbner/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChrisAbner/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChrisAbner/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":3045702973,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzMDQ1NzAyOTcz","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/labels/Category:%20Engine","name":"Category: Engine","color":"5319E7","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-10-30T03:14:11Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T22:36:56Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/pulls/25046","html_url":"https://github.com/php/php-src/pull/25046","diff_url":"https://github.com/php/php-src/pull/25046.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/php/php-src/pull/25046.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Fixes GH-24792.\n\nSince the VAR|TMP overhaul (6173a9a109), `zend_compile_var_inner()` compiles `ZEND_AST_ASSIGN` and `ZEND_AST_ASSIGN_REF` for every fetch type. When an assignment is the container of a write, such as `($a = [1])[0] = 2`, `unset(($a = [1])[0])` or `$r = &($a = [1])[0]`, the compiler emits a write fetch on the TMP result of the assignment. That combination has no handler, so the script compiles and then dies with `Invalid opcode`. PHP 8.5 rejected all of these at compile time with \"Cannot use temporary expression in write context\". This patch restores that error.\n\nThe overhaul added these cases so that a destructuring assignment with references can be passed by reference (`f([&$x] = $arr)`). It originally had an assertion limiting them to that case, which a01a8e72ac removed. The patch keeps compiling assignments when `by_ref` is set or when the fetch is not a write (`W`/`RW`/`UNSET`), and otherwise falls through to the existing `default` branch and its error. This puts the check in the one place every write container goes through. Checking in each caller (dim, prop, unset, inc/dec, reference fetch) would have needed one check per caller. As a side effect, `($a =& $b)[0] = 2` and `([&$x] = $arr)[0] = 5` are compile errors again. PHP 8.5 rejected them too; 8.6.0RC4 started executing them. If you would rather keep those working in 8.6, I can narrow the check.\n\n**Verification.** Debug NTS build of `PHP-8.6` (e2fa0c9f7f, `--disable-all --enable-cli`), compared with the official `php:8.5-cli` (8.5.12) and `php:8.6.0RC4-cli` images:\n\n| Code | 8.5.12 | 8.6.0RC4 | PHP-8.6 + patch |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `($a = [1])[0] = 2;` | compile error | `Invalid opcode 23/2/1` | compile error |\n| `($a = new stdClass)->p = 1;` | compile error | `Invalid opcode 24/2/1` | compile error |\n| `($a = [1])[0] += 2;` | compile error | `Invalid opcode 27/2/1` | compile error |\n| `($a = [1])[0]++;` | compile error | `Invalid opcode 87/2/1` | compile error |\n| `unset(($a = [1])[0]);` | compile error | `Invalid opcode 75/2/1` | compile error |\n| `$r = &($a = [1])[0];` | compile error | `Invalid opcode 84/2/1` | compile error |\n| `f(($a = [1])[0]);` with `f(&$x)` | compile error | `Invalid opcode 84/2/1` | compile error |\n| `($a =& $b)[0] = 2;` | compile error | runs | compile error |\n| `([&$x] = $arr)[0] = 5;` | compile error | runs | compile error |\n| `f([&$x] = $arr);` / `f($a =& $b);` with `f(&$x)` | works | works | works |\n| `isset(($a = [1])[0])`, `($a = [1])[5] ?? 'd'`, `($v = ['k' => 'v'])['k']` | works | works | works |\n\nOut of 30 variants in total, all 30 match 8.5.12 with the patch, with and without OPcache + tracing JIT. Without the patch, 15 fail with `Invalid opcode` in 8.6.0RC4 and on master.\n\n| Tests | Result |\n|---|---|\n| New `Zend/tests/gh24792*.phpt` (9) on 8.5.12 / 8.6.0RC4 / patched | 9 pass / 8 fail / 9 pass |\n| `Zend/tests` + `tests`, patched | 6301 passed, 0 failed |\n| `Zend/tests` + `tests` + `ext/opcache/tests`, patched, `opcache.enable_cli=1`, `opcache.jit=tracing`, `opcache.protect_memory=1` | 7275 passed, 0 failed |\n\nNot covered: `foreach (($a =& $b) as &$v) { $v = 3; }` writes through to `$b` in 8.5 but not in 8.6.0RC4, with or without this patch. It is a separate behaviour change from the same overhaul and is left alone here. I only tested on Linux x86_64 NTS debug builds, not ZTS or ASAN builds of the patch. The bug itself also reproduces on the official ZTS RC4 image.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/issues/25046/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/issues/25046/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0}],"search_type":"lexical"}